# ZUUP-OS firewall drop-in directory (spec §6.3) — the IMAGE-baked half.
#
# Two directories feed the base ruleset, and the difference between them is the
# difference between what a signing key controls and what a booted machine does:
#
#   /etc/zuup/nftables.d/          this one. Inside the dm-verity squashfs, so
#                                  its contents are covered by the Secure Boot
#                                  signature and are identical across the fleet.
#
#   /run/zuup-identity/nftables.d/ written at boot by zuup-identity.service from
#                                  the per-terminal parameters on the SIGNED
#                                  kernel cmdline. Different per machine;
#                                  authenticated by the UKI signature rather
#                                  than by being read-only.
#
# nft tolerates a glob that matches nothing (verified: both an empty directory
# and a missing one load cleanly), so neither include needs a placeholder to
# keep the firewall loading. This file therefore adds no rule and exists only to
# put the above where someone looking for it will find it.
#
# What lands in the /run directory, from the signed cmdline:
#
#   10-edge-peer.nft   add element inet zuup edge_lan { <zuup.edge> }
#   20-hq-egress.nft   add element inet zuup hq_dest  { <zuup.hq …> }
#                      — written ONLY when zuup.capability=ADMIN_STATION
